    "unit": 13,
    "title": "Nuance: Look vs Seem vs Appear",
    "title_ko": "뉘앙스: Look vs Seem vs Appear",
    "focus_axis": "vocabulary"
  },
  "context": {
    "explanation_en": "'Look' is about visual appearance ('You look tired'). 'Seem' is a general impression, not necessarily visual ('He seems nice'). 'Appear' is more formal/tentative, often used when the impression could be wrong ('The situation appears to be under control').",
    "explanation_ko": "'look'은 시각적 외양에 관한 것입니다('You look tired'). 'seem'은 시각적이지 않을 수도 있는 일반적인 인상입니다('He seems nice'). 'appear'는 더 격식적·잠정적이며, 인상이 틀릴 수도 있을 때 자주 쓰입니다('The situation appears to be under control').",
    "key_expressions": [
      {
        "en": "You look exhausted today.",
        "ko": "오늘 완전히 지쳐 보여요."
      },
      {
        "en": "She seems very kind.",
        "ko": "그녀는 아주 친절한 것 같아요."
      },
      {
        "en": "The plan appears to be working.",
        "ko": "그 계획이 효과가 있는 것으로 보여요."
      }
    ]
  },
